<http://data.silknow.org/object/d128e19b-65bd-3f51-91a5-fee38e9566fe/domain/3>
        a                    silk:T19 ;
        silk:L4              "Royalty" ;
        ecrm:P41_classified  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d128e19b-65bd-3f51-91a5-fee38e9566fe> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/d128e19b-65bd-3f51-91a5-fee38e9566fe/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "(original 1933 catalogue entry) Child's dress.  White silk.  The frock has a plain neck and fastens behind.  The bodice is pleated, the skirts are full and gathered to the waist.  The latter [the skirts] are decorated with a vertical row of buttons and three horizontal flounces terminating in a button in front where they turn and run up [to] the waist.  Short sleeves with double band and buttons.\nApparently the dress worn by King Edward VII when Prince of Wales, in the portrait by Winterhalter at Windsor Castle.  Cf the Crossley Mosaic panel T.61-1929."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/d128e19b-65bd-3f51-91a5-fee38e9566fe> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/d128e19b-65bd-3f51-91a5-fee38e9566fe/category/1>
